identify a threat  and neutralize it while still asleep it  doesn't get much more badass than that  when nezuko eventually uses her blood  demon art to wake  everyone up rangoku tells tanjiro that  he will defend the eight  train cars from enmu together with  nezuko and zenitsu  while tanjiro and inosuke go to the  front of the train to confront  enmu rengoku once again shows off what  an absolute legend he is  as he defends the back five cars all on  his own  leaving zenitsu and nezuko to take care  of just the front  three cars this makes perfect sense for  rengoku  because as a hashira he feels obligated  to handle most of the burden  on his own and his ability to protect 5  cars by himself  is a testament to his incredible speed  strength  and determination and in the end the  demon slayers managed to save  hundreds of innocent lives on the mugen  train something that would have been  impossible without  rengoku's extraordinary commitment after  tanjiro and inosuke managed to defeat  enemy upper moon 3 akaza makes his  appearance  and he attempts to kill tanjiro at this  point tanjiro is already injured as a  result of his fight with enmu  sorenguku steps up to protect tanjiro  and he takes  akaza head on akaza is very impressed  with rengoku's swordsmanship skills  and he invites rangoku to become a demon  like him  but rengoku instantly refuses he has  dedicated his life  to fighting demons and he has no  interest in becoming one of them and yet  akaza keeps trying to convince him to  become a demon after all  if rengoku turns into a demon then he  won't have to worry about death  and he can spend all of eternity  training to get stronger  akasa would love this because he loves  to fight strong opponents  and since rangoku is already strong even  as a human  he would have incredible potential if he  were to become a demon  akasa can't understand why anyone would  want to remain a weak human who is  doomed to lead a short life  and then die instead of becoming an  overpowered demon  who can live forever but rengoku says  that death  is the very thing that makes human life  so precious  and beautiful as rengoku puts it growing  old  and dying is what gives meaning and  beauty to the fleeting span of a human  life  it's precisely because we age and die  that our lives have value  and nobility akasa still doesn't get it  and he thinks that it would be a waste  for a gifted swordsman like rengoku to  die  so soon but rengoku doesn't think that  death is sad at all  death is only natural for human beings  and so whenever it may come  it is not to be feared rather death is a  perfectly normal part of life  at this point tanjiro attempts to help  rangoku in the fight against  akaza however rengoku tells tanjiro to  stay put  because he was already injured during  the fight with enmu and if his  wound reopens he will probably die  rengoku then proceeds to engage akuza in  combat  yet again and his skill and  determination truly impress  akaza eventually akaza manages to give  rengoku  a fatal wound by sticking his entire arm  through the hashida's stomach akaza then  tries to convince rengoku one last time  to become a demon if he doesn't decide  to become a demon now  he will definitely die from this wound  becoming a demon  is his only chance to save himself but  instead of entertaining akaza's proposal  rengoku decides to keep fighting against  akaza  despite this severe injury in fact  rengoku uses the wound  to his advantage the sun is about to  rise  and rengoku's plan is to keep akaza  right where he is  by keeping akaza's arm trapped inside  his  own stomach then once the sun rises and  makes contact with  akaza the demon will burn up and die  yes rengoku's wound will surely kill him  but he intends to do his duty as a  hashida one last time  by taking akaza down with him up to this  point  akaza was just impressed with rangoku's  strength and determination  but now akasa begins to really fear for  his own life  he does his best to break free from  rangoku's grip  but the hashira refuses to budge once  again he fights through the pain  just so he can fulfill his duty as  hashira now desperate  akaza cuts his own arms off in order to  escape from rengoku's grip  as rengoku drops down to his knees akaza  runs away  into the forest before the sun can reach  him  that is when we get an incredibly  emotional moment in which  tanjiro heartbroken about what just  happened to rengoku  throws his sword at the fleeing akaza  and screams at him to stop running away  like a coward tanjiro says that rengoku  is braver and more honorable than akaza  will ever be  because he fought to save the lives of  others until the very end and he didn't  run away like a coward  tanjiro says that rangoku won this fight  because even though akaza is alive and  rengoku is dying  akaza is running away while rengoku  stood his ground  and fought with honor until his very  last  breath and i have to agree with tanjiro  here  akasa as a demon is objectively stronger  than rengoku but even though rengoku was  fatally injured  he nearly killed akaza by forcing him to  face the sunlight  and in the end akaza ran away from the  fight  so akaza lost and rengoku won even  though this would sadly be  rengoku's final victory as he is dying  rengoku does not show fear or sadness  he stays true to his convictions until  the very end  and he even takes time to tell tanjiro  to visit the rengoku family home so that  he can learn more about the dance of the  fire god  he also asks tanjiro to tell his younger  brother to follow his own path  and to tell his father to take care of  himself just  think about that for a second even as he  is dying rangoku wants to help tanjiro  in his quest to learn more about the  dance of the fire god  and he also wants to encourage his  brother one last time  while sending kind words to his father  the same father who mistreated him and  discouraged him for his entire life  that is the kind of person that rengoku  is  he is always doing his best to help  others and he doesn't hold  any sort of grudge against his father in  fact  rengoku believes that his father acted  the way that he did because he was  worried about losing his two  sons rengoku's father knew from his own  experience as a former hashira  that being a demon slayer is extremely  dangerous  but because he is old-fashioned and  doesn't know how to show his true  emotions  he tried to discourage his sons from  putting themselves in danger  by telling them to just give up on  becoming demon slayers because they're  not  good enough he treated them this way not  because he hated them  but because he loved them and didn't  want to lose them  at least that is how rengoku interprets  it and again  i am in awe of the strength of this  man's character  most people would hate their father if  they were in rangoku's shoes  but rangoku is not most people  he is able to see the best in everyone  including his father  rengoku then looks tanjiro right in the  eye and says that after seeing how  nezuko was fighting to protect innocent  people  on board the train he now accepts her as  a member  of the demon slayer core that is a  complete reversal from his previous  stance  that all demons should be killed  immediately and that anyone who  cooperates with them should be punished  but this drastic change shows us that  rengoku is the kind of person who is  open to learning new things  and to changing his mind he is not  stubborn and stuck in his ways like so  many people  instead he is willing to learn from new  experiences and develop as a person  which is such an important quality for  anyone to have and so  after seeing nezuko risking her life to  protect humans from a fellow demon  rengoku understands that nezuko is  different and that she deserves  respect rengoku then tells tanjiro  zenitsu and inosuke that he believes in  them  as the next generation of hashira he  then tells them not to feel bad about  him dying  because as a hashira it is his duty to  give his own life to protect them  just as his comrades gave their lives to  protect him  during his very first mission rengoku  leaves tanjiro with  these words go ahead and live with your  head  held high no matter how devastated you  may be by your own weakness or  uselessness  set your heart ablaze grit your teeth  and look straight ahead wow  this was so powerful and it reminds me  of my favorite anime character of all  time  kamina those of you who have seen guren  lagann know exactly what i'm talking  about  in his final moments rengoku sees a  vision of his mother  and he asks her whether he did a good  job in keeping the promise that he had  made to her  she tells him that he did a wonderful  job and as he is about to die  rengoku smiles earlier on rengoku said  that death  is not something to fear it is a  perfectly natural part of life  and in fact death is the very thing that  makes human life  so precious in the end rengoku stayed  true to his own philosophy  and to his principles and not only did  he willingly die to protect his comrades  but he died with a smile on his face  without  any fear or sadness and even though  rengoku died a noble death  at this relatively early point in the  story his legacy  definitely didn't die with him rengoku  sacrificed his life in order to save  tanjiro and tanjiro would eventually go  on to defeat  muzon without rengoku's sacrifice  tanjiro would have died here  and muzon would not have been defeated  but more than that  rengoku sacrifice inspired tanjiro  zenitsu inosuke  and many others and it drove them to  become the incredible demon slayers that  they would eventually become  so when you really think about it  despite being a side character who died  relatively early on rengoku ended up  playing a really important role  in the overall story and i'm so glad  that this was the case  because rengaku is both a great hashira  and  a wonderful human being and that 